o, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,-1,2)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(1,-1,2)+∇f(1,-1,2)\\cdot ⟨x-1,y+1,z-2⟩ \\\\  & =f(1,-1,2)+⟨{f}_{x}(1,-1,2),{f}_{y}(1,-1,2),{f}_{z}(1,-1,2)⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y+1,z-2⟩ \\\\  & =6+⟨-4,-1,3⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y+1,z-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(1.04,-0.99,2.02)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=1.04,$ $y=-0.99,$ and $z=2.02$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.04,-0.99,2.02) & ≈6+⟨-4,-1,3⟩\\cdot ⟨1.04-1,-0.99+1,2.02-2⟩ \\\\  & =6+⟨-4,-1,3⟩\\cdot ⟨0.04,0.01,0.02⟩ \\\\  & =6-0.16-0.01+0.06 \\\\  & =5.89\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420918 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186420931 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420918 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186420932 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420918 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186420933 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420918 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186420934 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420918 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186420935 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420918 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420918 #edb/ref 1045 "Linearization of Multivariable Functions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420918 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186420933 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420918 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046659 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420918 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049809 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420918 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "e616bf48-afee-5693-88d5-4ed73b51c3cc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420919 #edb/ref 1080 "f(x,y)≈-2x-y" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420919 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420919 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "19a5d7fe-a63b-5e32-949d-b3f2969e0db8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420920 #edb/ref 1080 "f(x,y,z)≈\\pi -1-x-z" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420920 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420920 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3996a57d-3ca8-5